  "description": "T7777. Lime Tree. Approximately 13 metres in height. Remove basal growth to inspect the base of the tree. Re pollard tree back to previous points. Tree has become very overgrown and touching the building and overhanging a residential garden/ blocking sunlight. Re pollarding will ensure a more compact shape, and to stop fallen debris. Situated by 27 Prince of Wales Dr by the entrance. T7778. Sycamore Tree. Approximately 16 metres in height. 12 metres in width. Full inspection is not possible as Ivy clad. Cut back from building by 2 metres, leaving the tree 10 metre. Tree has become very overgrown and now touching the building. Situated by the entrance along Rosenau Road. T7882. Tree is dead so unable to identify. Approximately 5/6 metres in height. Fell to ground level. Tree is situated in the rear communal garden. T7783. Tree is dead so unable to identify. Approximately 3/4 metres in height. Fell to ground level. Tree is situated in the rear communal garden. T7800. Lime Tree. 14 metres in height. Reduce by 3 metres, leaving the tree 11 metres in height. Trees have become very overgrown and blocking sunlight. deadwood with aim of phased removal. 50% dysfunctional bark at the base, reduced vigour. Situated along Albert Bridge Road"
